<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Governance's cross-section surface, carved into its own leaf project because most of its
    consumers are still in Base: OnboardingService, DashboardService, AdminDashboardService and
    ConsentService read through IApplicationServiceRead / IMembershipCalculatorRead,
    SystemTeamSyncJob, SuspendNonCompliantMembersJob, SendReConsentReminderJob and
    HumansMetricsService do the same from Humans.Infrastructure, and TermRenewalReminderJob
    drives the three renewal members. A Contracts/ *folder* inside Humans.Governance would
    therefore make Base reference a section and cycle (design §15.5b,
    memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md).

    It holds exactly what lives outside the section: the tier-application read surface, the
    three members the renewal job needs, the membership-calculator read surface, the DTOs
    those signatures name, and ApplicationStatus — which cannot follow the entities into the
    section's internal Domain/ because UserApplicationSnapshot names it and so do a dozen Base
    and Shell read paths (design §15 step 5, Budget's rule).

    G5 lane 4b-2k added MembershipStatus and MembershipStatusLabels here. MembershipStatus is
    named by this leaf's own MembershipSnapshot (Budget's rule); MembershipStatusLabels came
    with it because its only consumer is Humans.UI's StatusBadgeExtensions, and Base can name a
    leaf but not a section project.

    References Humans.Interfaces (IApplicationService) and Humans.Domain, the latter now for
    MembershipTier alone — the design doc's "UserInfo object graph" ruling sends that one to
    Humans.Users.Contracts in lane 3d, and this edge dies with it. Same pair
    Humans.Campaigns.Contracts takes. Acyclic: Humans.Domain names only Humans.Interfaces.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Domain\Humans.Domain.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NodaTime" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
